.TH SDL_GetTrayEntries 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetTrayEntries \- Returns a list of entries in the menu, in order.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_tray.h>
.PP
.BI "const SDL_TrayEntry ** SDL_GetTrayEntries(SDL_TrayMenu *menu, int *count);
.fi
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I menu
The menu to get entries from\[char46]
.TP
.I count
An optional pointer to obtain the number of entries in the menu\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a NULL-terminated list of entries within the given menu\[char46] The pointer becomes invalid when any function that inserts or deletes entries in the menu is called\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should be called on the thread that created the tray\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_RemoveTrayEntry (3),
.BR SDL_InsertTrayEntryAt (3)
